# 2026-05-03 21:18:30.334840
+In app/Http/Middleware/SecurityHeaders.php, fix the Content Security Policy header so that Vite's dev server is allowed in local development only.
+Find the line that sets the Content-Security-Policy header. Replace it with logic that checks the environment:
+php$viteDevSources = app()->isLocal()
+    ? " http://localhost:5173 http://[::1]:5173 http://localhost:5194 http://[::1]:5194 ws://localhost:5173 ws://[::1]:5173 ws://localhost:5194 ws://[::1]:5194"
+    : '';
+
+$response->headers->set('Content-Security-Policy',
+    "default-src 'self';" .
+    "script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval'{$viteDevSources};" .
+    "style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'{$viteDevSources};" .
+    "img-src 'self' data: " . config('filesystems.disks.s3.url', '') . ";" .
+    "connect-src 'self' ws://" . config('app.reverb_host', 'localhost:8080') . " wss://" . config('app.reverb_host', 'localhost:8080') . "{$viteDevSources};" .
+    "font-src 'self';" .
+    "frame-ancestors 'none';"
+);
+In production app()->isLocal() returns false so $viteDevSources is an empty string and the CSP stays strict. In local development it adds the Vite dev server ports to the allowed sources so npm run dev works without CSP errors.
+Only edit app/Http/Middleware/SecurityHeaders.php. Do not touch any other files."

